## c2-px4 | Calc 2 drill: series and ODEs | maths | 2 | calc2 | c2-px3
quiz 3 | Sum of Σ (2/3)ⁿ from n = 0?
* 3
o 2
o 3/2
o ∞
= 1/(1 − 2/3).
> Next

quiz 3 | Σ 1/n^0.5 …
* Diverges
o Converges
o Converges to 2
= p = 1/2 ≤ 1.
> Next

quiz 4 | Does Σ (−1)ⁿ n/(n + 1) converge?
* No: terms don't go to zero
o Yes, conditionally
o Yes, absolutely
= n/(n + 1) → 1. Divergence test.
> Next

quiz 4 | Maclaurin series for sinh x?
* x + x³/3! + x⁵/5! + …
o x − x³/3! + x⁵/5! − …
o 1 + x²/2! + x⁴/4! + …
o 1 + x + x²/2! + …
= Same as sin x but all plus signs.
> Next

quiz 4 | Solve dy/dx = y/x.
* y = Cx
o y = Ceˣ
o y = C/x
o y = x + C
= Separable: ln|y| = ln|x| + c.
> Next

quiz 4 | Solve y′ + 2y = 0, y(0) = 5.
* y = 5e^(−2x)
o y = 5e^(2x)
o y = 2e^(−5x)
o y = 5 − 2x
= Exponential decay.
> Next

quiz 4 | General solution of y″ + 2y′ + 5y = 0?
* e^(−x)(A cos 2x + B sin 2x)
o Ae^(−x) + Be^(−5x)
o A cos 5x + B sin 5x
o (A + Bx)e^(−x)
= r² + 2r + 5 = 0, r = −1 ± 2i. Damped oscillation.
> Next

quiz 4 | L{1} = ?
* 1/s
o 1
o s
o 1/s²
= ∫₀^∞ e^(−st) dt.
> Next

quiz 4 | L{t} = ?
* 1/s²
o 1/s
o s
o 2/s³
= In general L{tⁿ} = n!/sⁿ⁺¹.
> Next

quiz 4 | Fourier series of an even function contains only…
* Cosine terms (and a constant)
o Sine terms
o Both always
o Neither
= Cosines are even; sines are odd.
> Calc 2 drill complete

